{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["The reason for <b>which you did not know, nor did your fathers know</b>: it is that you did not know through the manna that you could live many days, nor had such reached you by tradition from your fathers. Or it may be said: He performed with you this great kindness which your holy fathers did not attain, for even though they went after Him according to all that He commanded them — לך לך מארצך וממולדתך ומבית אביך (Genesis 12:1) — their merit did not reach the level that He would sustain them with the grain of heaven, as He did for you. Thus they said in Midrash Bemidbar Sinai Rabbah (Numbers Rabbah 1:2): In the merit of Moses you ate the manna — something your holy fathers did not see, as it is stated, ולא ידעון אבתיך. And He explained that He did this to make known that He gives life to man through whatever He decrees; if so, keep His commandments and live. And it is possible to interpret that ויענך וירעיבך ויאכלך את המן are distinct matters: he says that He afflicted you in your journeying through the wilderness forty years, like the sense of ענה בדרך כחי (Psalms 102:24), and He made you hungry at first, as they said (Exodus 16:3) 'to put this whole congregation to death by starvation,' and afterward He fed you the manna to make known to you that not by bread alone does man live but by every word that proceeds from the mouth of HaShem — and so המאכילך מן במדבר אשר לא ידעון אבתיך (Deuteronomy 8:16), recounting the miracle He performed for them. And <b>in order to afflict you</b> returns to המוליכך במדבר הגדל והנורא וגו' וצמאון וגו' (Deuteronomy 8:15). But what He said in the section of the manna (Exodus 16:4), למען אנסנו הילך בתורתי אם לא — that I will give them their needs and bring their requests to them and see whether they will obey Me when goodness abounds — this goes according to the plain sense, but the first interpretation is true and correct."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:46:54.572056092Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}